19905.docs:
The layout of `src`, or why it has none; `None` until [`EquationCache::refresh`] has run
for this source. A source over [`crate::math::MAX_SOURCE_BYTES`] is answered at once,
whatever the entry holds, by its length alone.

26188.docs:
Whether the compound file holds an encryption stream. Walks the directory through the FAT;
when the structure can't be followed (truncated or malformed), falls back to scanning the
bytes for the UTF-16LE stream names.

9657.docs:
`name`, or `name (2)`, `name (3)`… if a macro already has it, a kept one too. A free name comes back as it is;
a renamed one is shortened to make room for the suffix, so it stays within
[`crate::model::MAX_MACRO_NAME`] characters. The result still goes through [`check`].

4321.docs:
Formulas that use a renamed name follow it: cell formulas and other names' definitions, on
the sheets where `old` resolves to the renamed name (its own sheet for a sheet-scoped name;
every sheet without a same-named sheet-level name for a workbook-level one).

15472.docs:
SUMIF / AVERAGEIF: matched numbers from the sum range, read at the criteria range's positions.
Excel sizes a sum range reference like the criteria range, anchored at its own top-left cell;
the evaluator does that resizing (it has the references), so cells line up one to one here.
